# Client-side Supabase config (both values are public by design; real .env is
# still gitignored so environments can differ)
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://euzjcejbkxvqfrttgaxu.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_xu398Mifx_w42hnJzcD2GA_lxRfVS43

# Origin of the Cloudflare Worker in cloudflare/identity-gateway/ — the only
# route a Game Center assertion may take to Supabase. The value below is a
# PLACEHOLDER on purpose: the deployed origin, the Worker's ALLOWED_ORIGINS
# value, and the order the whole rollout happens in live in docs/IDENTITY.md
# ("Game Center remains one held owner rollout"), not in a committed example.
#
# Unset or empty is not a safe default, it is a silent disable. src/config.ts
# falls back to '', the client posts to a relative /v1/game-center that nothing
# serves, and the profile never offers to link Game Center. Nothing is logged.
#
# Vite inlines it at BUILD time, so it must be set where each surface is built,
# not where it runs:
#   web    - the Cloudflare Pages project's environment variables, for every
#            environment that builds (production and preview)
#   native - the shell that runs `npm run build` before `native:sync:ios` or
#            `native:sync:android`; the value is baked into native/www/
#
# Never add GC_AUTH_ORIGIN_SECRET or any other secret as a VITE_ variable: a
# VITE_ value is inlined into the shipped bundle and is public.
VITE_IDENTITY_GATEWAY_URL=https://identity.example.workers.dev
